<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cornelis Lampsins</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1600">1600</a>–<a href="/years/1664">1664</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Cornelis Lampsins was a merchant and burgomaster of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vlissingen">Vlissingen</a> in Zeeland. With his brother Adriaan he sponsored the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> colonisation of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tobago">Tobago</a> from 1654, settling planters and enslaved Africans there. In 1662 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-xiv">Louis XIV</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> made him Baron of Tobago, though the colony remained Dutch-run and was destroyed in the Anglo-Dutch and Franco-Dutch wars.</p></div>
